WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:06.730
With twisted-pair Ethernet cable, there are
two wiring standards: 568a and 568b.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:12.810
In 568a, pins 1 and 2 are white/green and
green, pins 3 and 6 are white/orange and orange,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:18.640
pins 4 and 5 are blue and white/blue, and
pins 7 and 8 are white/brown and brown.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.419
In a 568b standard, pins 1 and 2 are white/orange
and orange and pins 3 and 6 are white/green

00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:24.419
and green.

00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:28.279
A straight-through cable, which represents
most Ethernet cables, is used to connect unlike

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:32.230
devices to each other, like a PC to a switch
or a router.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.900
When two like devices are connected to each
other, a crossover cable is used.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:40.740
The reason for that is that when two like
devices are connected, they both want to send

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.230
and receive on the same wires, which will
cause many collisions of data.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:50.070
Thus, the four wires primarily used for transmission
are crossed over so the data can transmit

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.320
freely from one device to another.

